   reset-to-initial-trusted-set assertion. Mutation: temporarily changed
   reset to reapply current rather than initial admission. Both assertions
   failed (5 tests, 31 assertions, 2 failures, 0 errors, exit 1). Restored
   the implementation immediately and inspected git diff. No mutation left.
3. Documentation only: 7.5.8 describes the landed holder context and REPL
   commands in present tense. AL-2 excludes protocol state under :admission,
   while allowing configuration. No linker implementation edits.
4. Own untrust: prints \"Own principal p is always trusted\" and returns the
   unchanged state, including when own is explicitly in the trusted set.
   Both display and state assertions were red before the fix.
5. Principal errors: shared parser says \"invalid principal id: expected
   ed25519:...\". Updated the CLI error assertion and added a REPL assertion
   for neutral wording. Flag help is unchanged. REPL assertions were red
